---
args: { input: CaseInput }
returns: RunProposal
---
1. Bind `goal = await frameRequest(input)` from the request and `policy = await selectPolicy(input)` from supplied authority candidates. Preserve unresolved precedence instead of guessing which source governs.
2. Bind `work = await formTaskGraph(goal)` and `evidencePlan = await planEvidence(input, work)` so each operation has explicit prerequisites and a searched source universe.
3. Run the stages in their dependency order. The first stage receives only `input.domainRecords.firstStage`; every later stage receives the preceding function's actual accepted records. Bind each full result separately.
const assessFitResult = await assessFit(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan);
const diagnoseStructureResult = await diagnoseStructure(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, assessFitResult.accepted);
const designCategoryRevisionResult = await designCategoryRevision(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, diagnoseStructureResult.accepted);
const simulateReclassificationResult = await simulateReclassification(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, designCategoryRevisionResult.accepted);
const promoteTaxonomyResult = await promoteTaxonomy(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, simulateReclassificationResult.accepted);
4. Bind `stageSet: CaseStageSet = { assessFit: assessFitResult, diagnoseStructure: diagnoseStructureResult, designCategoryRevision: designCategoryRevisionResult, simulateReclassification: simulateReclassificationResult, promoteTaxonomy: promoteTaxonomyResult }` and `collection: CollectionFinding = await reconcileCollection(stageSet)`. Bind `allQuestions: string[] = [...assessFitResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...diagnoseStructureResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...designCategoryRevisionResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...simulateReclassificationResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...promoteTaxonomyResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...collection.coverageGaps]` and `questions: QuestionBatch = await resolveQuestions(allQuestions, input)`.
5. Bind `invalidation = await assessDelta(input)`, `review = await prepareReview(collection)`, and `view = await composeView(review, input)`; pass each child its actual declared inputs and retain the returned object.
6. Bind `allChecks: CheckResult[] = [...assessFitResult.checks, ...diagnoseStructureResult.checks, ...designCategoryRevisionResult.checks, ...simulateReclassificationResult.checks, ...promoteTaxonomyResult.checks]`. Bind `hasGateFailure = allChecks.some(check => check.verdict !== "pass")` and `hasBlocker = input.authorityStatus !== "authorized" || questions.questions.length > 0 || collection.coverageGaps.length > 0`. Bind `disposition: "proposed" | "blocked" | "needs-review" = hasBlocker ? "blocked" : hasGateFailure ? "needs-review" : "proposed"`. Bind `rationale: string[] = allChecks.map(check => `${check.check}: ${check.verdict}; evidence ${check.evidenceIds.join(",")}`)`.
7. Operational detail 1 — A category is renamed without semantic change: retain its ID and avoid unnecessary reclassification. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (retain its ID and avoid unnecessary reclassification.) through the existing stage result for CategoryFit; preserve exact source/version and the prior CategoryFit, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
8. Operational detail 2 — A split cannot be reconstructed historically: report a coarser comparable series. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (report a coarser comparable series.) through the existing stage result for CategoryFit; preserve exact source/version and the prior CategoryFit, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
9. Operational detail 3 — A downstream system accepts only one label: expose incompatibility with a new multi-label rule. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (expose incompatibility with a new multi-label rule.) through the existing stage result for CategoryFit; preserve exact source/version and the prior CategoryFit, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
10. Operational detail 4 — A rare concept is important despite low frequency: allow evidence-based exceptions to frequency heuristics. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (allow evidence-based exceptions to frequency heuristics.) through the existing stage result for CategoryFit; preserve exact source/version and the prior CategoryFit, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
11. Operational detail 5 — Two stewards edit related branches: detect semantic boundary conflicts before merging. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (detect semantic boundary conflicts before merging.) through the existing stage result for CategoryFit; preserve exact source/version and the prior CategoryFit, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
12. Initialize `revisions: RevisionProposal[] = []`. If any gate is not pass, bind `revision = await proposeRevision(the failed check names, the smallest affected stage name)` and add that returned proposal to revisions. Bind and return `result: RunProposal = { caseId: input.caseId, goal, policy, work, evidencePlan, assessFit: assessFitResult, diagnoseStructure: diagnoseStructureResult, designCategoryRevision: designCategoryRevisionResult, simulateReclassification: simulateReclassificationResult, promoteTaxonomy: promoteTaxonomyResult, collection, questions, invalidation, review, view, revisions, disposition, rationale }`. Proposed actions remain proposals. The host owns authorization, persistence, effect dispatch and verification.
